    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. My concern is that if we don't have a strict system in place immediately, things will just get lost in the shuffle or end up in a mess that's hard to clean up later. Do you have any advice for preventing that kind of mess from becoming permanent or \"taking over\" the archival space?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To prevent long-term archival disorder, implement a robust, layered intake workflow regardless of the classification system chosen. Begin with comprehensive physical control using unique, sequential accession numbers attached to every item immediately upon receipt. Only after this fundamental physical tracking is established should staff begin the slower, more detailed process of applying LCC or DDC categorization. This separation routine ensures accountability without forcing premature, potentially inaccurate intellectual organization.",
